      "description": "Watch St. Truiden vs Lommel SK highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League clash between St. Truiden and Lommel SK promised a tactical battle from the opening whistle. Both sides took to the pitch with high energy, looking to secure a vital result in front of a passionate crowd. Lommel Strikes First from the Spot On August 10, 2026 , the match began with a cagey atmosphere as both teams felt each other out. The deadlock was broken in the 24th minute when the referee awarded a penalty to Lommel SK . Veteran striker Ralf Seuntjens stepped up to the spot and clinicaly dispatched his effort into the net, giving the visitors a crucial lead. Lommel managed to maintain their defensive shape for the remainder of the first half, frustrating the home side's attempts to find an immediate response. Sebaoui Levels the Scoring The second half saw St. Truiden emerge with renewed purpose, utilizing their bench early to inject fresh legs into the midfield. Their persistence paid off in the 64th minute. A brilliant piece of play from Nelson Ishiwatari saw him provide a perfectly weighted assist for Ilias Sebaoui , who made no mistake in finding the target. The equalizer shifted the momentum significantly, as St. Truiden began to dictate the tempo of the game while Lommel scrambled to regain their footing. A Dramatic Conclusion As the clock ticked toward the final whistle, the match became increasingly physical. Nelson Ishiwatari , who had been instrumental in the equalizer, received a yellow card in the 75th minute as the intensity peaked. Managers on both sides introduced several substitutes, including Oumar Diouf and Shion Shinkawa , in an attempt to find a late winner. Despite nine minutes of stoppage time, neither side could find the decisive breakthrough, and the match concluded at 90+9' with the points shared."
